        {
          "id": 1176640002,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Ah, you are right, the RFC and the ETSI standard just completely contradict each other, as you said. The RFC even says that the string can be UTF-8. My apologies.\n\nThat is odd.\n\nIn practice, I have generally seen it according to the 3GPP encoding, which is what is used on the original file that was fuzzed",
