  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "e9c6c448da3d516683d2f2d9b899ed4d2d56f94e",
      "short_id": "e9c6c448",
      "created_at": "2022-11-18T10:58:42.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "45c15019ac156f5bb5ad1a39caa2f8717aa472f2"
      ],
      "title": "mip6: Use ENC_APN_STR",
      "message": "mip6: Use ENC_APN_STR\n\nRFC 5149 implies that Service Identifier strings should be\nUTF-8. 3GPP TS 29.275 states that they are encoded as APNs,\nsimilar to RFC 1035 (DNS labels). We guess what is used\nbased on a heuristic.\n\nUse ENC_APN_STR for the APN encoding rather than reimplementing\nit, as that handles invalid encodings better.\n\nFix #18647\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-11-17T10:37:59.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "João Valverde",
      "committer_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "committed_date": "2022-11-18T10:58:42.000+00:00",
